    "doc": "A line scan for one or more motors.\n\nArgs:\n    *args (device: DeviceBase, start: float, stop: float): repeated scan argument bundles.\n    steps (int): steps.\n    relative (bool): Whether the positions are relative to the current position.\n    exp_time (float [s]): Exposure time in seconds. Default: 0 s\n    frames_per_trigger (int): Number of frames per trigger for devices that support configurable frame counts per trigger. Default: 1\n    settling_time (float [s]): Time to settle before trigger and readout. Default: 0 s\n    settling_time_after_trigger (float [s]): Time to settle after the trigger but before the readout. Default: 0 s\n    readout_time (float [s]): Configuration for devices that support configurable readout times. Default: 0 s\n    burst_at_each_point (int): Number of triggers and readouts at each point. Default: 1\n\nReturns:\n    ScanReport\n\nExamples:\n    Minimum:\n        >>> scans.line_scan(dev.device1, -1.0, 1.0, steps=10, relative=False)\n    Full:\n        >>> scans.line_scan(dev.device1, -1.0, 1.0, steps=10, relative=False, exp_time=0, frames_per_trigger=1, settling_time=0, settling_time_after_trigger=0, readout_time=0, burst_at_each_point=1)",
